Z||000011||Monkeyman||01-09-2000||05:24 AM||||First of all, Jeff Gordon is a great driver.  He's not really my hero, though.  There are greater drivers in my mind such as A J Foyt.  I do like Jeff.  He has a good attitude about all aspects of racing.  He's just as good a loser as he is a winner which means more to me than the fact that he generally *is* a winner.  As far as the Lowenbrau...It's by far my favorite and most places don't have it.  Some haven't even heard of it.<P>x cuda man--According to everything I've ever read, J G has a small "collection" of vehicles.  Not only does he have an NSX, but also a Hummer (American made and the official vehicle of the US military), an original Ford GT40, a Ferrari, a couple of pickups, as well as some bad-a** GM rolling stock.  I'm not against ricers (the vehicles), I prefer Fieros.  Of course, my second choice is anything English and nothing seems to be truly "American made" anymore.||||reg||1
Z||000012||x cuda man||01-09-2000||01:05 PM||||just have to see how jeff does this year.(with all the changes at hendrick motorsports going on)he may be one of the most talented drivers ever!i,just like alot of people get sick of seeing him win so much!as far as the rice thing goes,the only brand new car i ever bought was a 86 CIVIC SI and i stil have it.it needs a little work because its been parked along time(1990).back in 86 i wanted a GT FIERO but the price was more than i wanted to spend so i shifted to the CRX SI,my girlfriend at the time had a kid,we got married so then i needed a back seat,so i got the CIVIC SI it's funny how thing's come around full circle,having just bought a 86 SE FIERO.  ||||reg||7
Z||000013||olympic||01-09-2000||07:49 PM||||   What a riot! I hav't laughed so much in a long time. I especially like the part where he riced up his computer with some stripes and an intel inside logo.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The stripe and huge exhaust tip thing has even hit small town Saskatchewan. They put them on everything from Sunbirds to Jettas. I still wonder who was the first person to hear a 4 cylinder engine with straight pipes and think to himself "wow, that sounds cool"??? To me, nothing sounds better than a 455 with a quadrajet carb at full throttle.||||reg||10
Z||000014||Cooter||01-09-2000||08:00 PM||||People around here are getting in the Ricer state of mind. Wheels all sticking out from under the fenders, straight pipe exhaust etc... One got behind me a while back while I was sitting in the drive through in my 'Burb. He was racing his engine and stereo was booming. Bad for him because my truck exhaust was right at his lowered window. I bumped the 'Burb into neutral and really dogged it-fuel injected 454 with headers, flow masters and 2.5 inch pipe. When I finally got to the window, the girl there smiled and thanked me for making the guy be quite!||||reg||1
